==Party listings==
The two parties' campaign committees (the [[National Republican Congressional Committee]] and [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]]) published their own lists of targeted seats.

===Republican-held seats===
On April 8, 2025, the [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]] released their target seat list which included Republican-held seats and open seats.<ref>{{cite web |last=rice@dccc.org |date=2025-04-08 |title=DCCC Announces 2026 Districts in Play |url=https://dccc.org/dccc-announces-2026-districts-in-play/ |access-date=2025-08-25 |website=DCCC |language=en-US}}</ref> On December 10, 2025, the list was revised adding four districts (CA-48, FL-15, NC-3, and NC-11) and removing two (CA-40 and CA-41).<ref>{{cite web |last=iwata@dccc.org |date=2025-12-10 |title=DCCC Expands the Battlefield in 2026 with New Offensive Targets |url=https://dccc.org/dccc-expands-the-battlefield-in-2026-with-new-offensive-targets/ |access-date=2025-12-11 |website=DCCC |language=en-US}}</ref> It was revised again on February 10, 2026, where five more districts (CO-5, MN-1, MT-1, SC-1, and VA-5) were added.<ref>{{cite web |last=iwata@dccc.org |date=2026-02-10 |title=DCCC Announces Second Expansion of the House Battlefield for 2026 Cycle with 5 New Offensive Targets |url=https://dccc.org/dccc-announces-second-expansion-of-the-house-battlefield-for-2026-cycle-with-5-new-offensive-targets/ |access-date=2026-02-10 |website=DCCC |language=en-US}}</ref> A subsequent revision on July 9, 2026, added one district (FL-16) and removed one district (FL-15).<ref>{{Cite web |last=rbaron@dccc.org |date=2026-07-09 |title=DCCC Adds Florida's 16th Congressional District To Districts In Play As Democrats Expand Battlefield for 2026 Midterms |url=https://dccc.org/dccc-adds-floridas-16th-congressional-district-to-districts-in-play-as-democrats-expand-battlefield-for-2026-midterms/ |access-date=2026-07-22 |website=DCCC |language=en-US}}</ref> Another subsequent revision occurred on August 5, 2026, where eleven more districts (AR-2, CO-3, CO-4, FL-12, IN-5, NC-9, NE-1, NV-2, NY-1, NY-21, and TX-23) were added to the list.<ref>{{Cite web |last=jalango@dccc.org |date=2026-08-05 |title=90 Days Out from the Midterms, DCCC Announces Latest Expansion of the House Battlefield for 2026 Cycle with 12 New Offensive Targets |url=https://dccc.org/90-days-out-from-the-midterms-dccc-announces-latest-expansion-of-the-house-battlefield-for-2026-cycle-with-12-new-offensive-targets/ |access-date=2026-08-05 |website=DCCC |language=en-US}}</ref> One last revision occurred on October 2, 2026, where seven more districts (KS-2, MI-1, NC-13, NJ-2, OK-5, VA-6, and WA-5) were added.<ref>{{Cite web |last=jalango@dccc.org |date=2026-10-02 |title=Just Over 30 Days from the Midterms, DCCC Announces Eight New Districts to Our Offensive House Battlefield |url=https://dccc.org/just-over-30-days-from-the-midterms-dccc-announces-eight-new-districts-to-our-offensive-house-battlefield/ |access-date=2026-10-03 |website=DCCC |language=en-US}}</ref>

